  "application_type_full": "Householder planning & demolition in a conservation area",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The &#x27;Art Studio&#x27; hereby permitted shall not be occupied at any time other than for purposes ancillary to the residential use of the dwelling known as The Albion, 36 Lauriston Road. REASON: In the interest of amenity use.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;The following shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the LPA prior to the commencement of the relevant part of the works. The work shall be carried out in accordance with the details so approved, and shall be maintained as such thereafter.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Details and samples of all proposed external materials, fixtures and finishes&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Details of all proposed external windows, doors and rooflights including the material, colour, finish, product information if available, and large scale drawings of each window (elevations at 1:20, sections and details at 1:5, showing the window and its surround/reveal)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Details of all proposed external boundary treatments/fences/balustrades/railings including the material, colour and finish, and larger scale plan, elevation and typical section drawings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Details of proposed landscaping including hard landscaping and planting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reason: In order to protect the special interest of the listed building and/or the character and appearance of the conservation area.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
